Undoable guest writes. PS2Memory::beginGuestSnapshot / endGuestSnapshot let code run on the side (an enhancement that draws more with the game's own draw code) and leave guest memory as it was: RDRAM is allocated page-aligned, and between the two calls the first write to each page saves it (Windows: pages made read-only, a vectored exception handler saves and opens a page at its first write, so the cost follows the pages written; elsewhere the whole block is copied); the scratchpad and the deterministic timer 0 state (patch 0154) are kept too. endGuestSnapshot puts it all back. Only the thread that began it may write meanwhile (a write from another thread waits until the end). runtime/ps2_guest_snapshot.h has the tracking itself.

